=============== FINDINGS (evidence limits; no exit-code effect) ==============
  - Live.Application.get_minor_version is never called, in any shape. Cause: D:\Projects\skeer-audio\autostem\tools\live-probe\AutoStemProbe\__init__.py:143 reads report["environment"]["live_version"] as self._call(app, "get_major_version", "get_minor_version"), and _call's signature is (target, method, *args) - so the second name arrives as an ARGUMENT to get_major_version(), which takes none. On a real Live _call catches the TypeError and the report carries an error line instead of a version; the call recorded here shows the wrong arity. Stage 0 does not read live_version, so the fork answer is unaffected. REPORTED, NOT FIXED: this brief forbids editing the probe.
  - Live.Application.get_application IS called and is not one of the three documented readers: the probe cannot reach an Application object without it. It takes no arguments, returns the handle and reads nothing from the set, so it is permitted with that reason. The ad-hoc harness this file replaces never instrumented it, so its "three names" could not have been complete; the honest allowlist for the shipped bytes is four.
  - Live.Application.get_menu_item_info is stage 2's fallback read (D:\Projects\skeer-audio\autostem\tools\live-probe\AutoStemProbe\__init__.py:191). The loop breaks once get_menu_info answers, so it never fires on a Live that has get_menu_info, and it is deliberately NOT in the allowlist: if a build lacks get_menu_info, this harness reddens with exit 4 by design and that name has to be added with the same read-only reason.
  - stub signatures are not Live's: the recorders accept any arguments, which is how the wrong-arity read above was visible as a call rather than as a TypeError. A real Live answers for itself; nothing here proves what Live's builtins accept, only what this script asks for.

